  "notes": "The heritage study for Rayy records a roughly 33 by 22 m historic shrine enclosure in the rock and stout southern masonry domes. The exact Qualla original shows six arched windows, a geometrically pierced parapet and the near stone retaining wall. The mapped dome sits on the southern end behind the longest facade."
